in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Silent Letters in English "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You don't say every letter in a word in English pronunciation. Some letters are silent, which means that you don't hear them as you would pronounce them normally."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are examples of the silent letter <span class=\"italic\">b</span> in words. Practice saying the example sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Letter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pronunciation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Silent B\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" climb<br/><br/>   comb<br/><br/>  dumb<br/><br/>    doubt<br/><br/>  limbs<br/><br/>  numb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"clime <br/><br/>  cohme<br/><br/>  dum<br/><br/> dowt <br/><br/>  lim<br/><br/>  num\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I had to <span class=\\\"strong\\\">climb</span> the stairs.<br/><br/> I didn't have time to <span class=\\\"strong\\\">comb</span> my hair.<br/><br/> I kept saying <span class=\\\"strong\\\">dumb</span> things.<br/><br/> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">doubt</span> that she found me interesting.<br/><br/><br/> My <span class=\\\"strong\\\">limbs</span> became <span class=\\\"strong\\\">numb</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Linking and Deletion with Must  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When a word ending in consonant +/t/ links into a word beginning with a consonant, the final /t/ of the first word is often deleted. This is often the case with the word must."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you delete (or drop) the final /t/, the sound before the /t/ must link smoothly into the following word."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  When the word have follows <span class=\"italic\">must</span>,  have is reduced to \"_ov\" or \"_av\".<br/> The 't' sound joins the reduced <span class=\"italic\">have</span>. <br/><br/>must have   =  mus_tuv or mus_tav "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Pronunciation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" mus_find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" mus_be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must have thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_tuv thought<br/>mus_ta thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must be happy to have met a girl who likes the same things as you!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She must have thought I was just a boring guy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She must have felt like I was just a waste of her time."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dumb"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " stupid; foolish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was so nervous that I kept saying dumb things all evening."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": 